#. §4: `h : transparencySymmetric.Stronger transparencyIncremental`
#: Game/Levels/Map/L03_ANewCut.lean:8
msgid "A cut is a comparison that fails, §0: some context accepts a sentence by §1 and\n"
"rejects it by §2. The library proves that incremental Transparency is stronger than Limited\n"
"Symmetry, and that symmetric Transparency is not. From these, show that symmetric Transparency is\n"
"not stronger than incremental Transparency.\n"
"\n"
"Begin with §3. If §4 held,\n"
"chaining it with the edge would give a comparison that the cut rules out."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Laws/L04_DoubleNegation.lean:13
msgid "A doubly negated conjunction has the value of the conjunction in the other order."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/OrderMatters/L01_FalsityFirst.lean:15
msgid "A false conjunct followed by an undefined one gives a false conjunction."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/TruthTables/L02_FalseAndUndefined.lean:18
msgid "A false conjunct settles a conjunction, so the failed presupposition of the other conjunct does not\n"
"make it undefined. In Strong Kleene logic this holds with the false conjunct in either position."
msgstr ""

