#. §2: `min b a`
#. §3: `rfl`
#. §4: `a`
#. §5: `b`
#: Game/Levels/TruthTables/L04_EveryRow.lean:8
msgid "A law of conjunction holds for every combination of values. With three values a law in two\n"
"variables has nine rows in its truth table, few enough for Lean to check them all. The tactic\n"
"§0 does this: it evaluates a statement about finitely many cases and closes the goal when\n"
"every case comes out true.\n"
"\n"
"The law below is commutativity: §1 and §2 agree for every pair of values. §3 cannot\n"
"prove it, since with §4 and §5 unknown there is nothing to compute."
msgstr ""

