msgid "A map of theories"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Map/L03_ANewCut.lean:6
msgid "A new cut"
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:10
msgid "A sentence whose presupposition fails, such as *the king of France is bald*, is neither true nor\n"
"false in a trivalent semantics. This game introduces the proof assistant Lean through that idea.\n"
"The first three worlds work with three truth values and the conjunctions that combine them, the\n"
"fourth applies them to sentences, and the last two compare theories of presupposition projection\n"
"with each other and with an experiment.\n"
"\n"
"Apart from a three-situation model for the examples, every definition and theorem in the game\n"
"comes from linglib, a Lean library of formal linguistics, so the objects you prove things about\n"
"are the ones its analyses use.\n"
"\n"
"Click on a world to start."
msgstr ""

