#: Game/Levels/Sentences/L02_FilteringByDefinition.lean:8
msgid "A theory of projection says when a context, a set of situations, accepts a sentence. Linglib\n"
"defines Peters's account, §0, in one line: a context accepts a sentence when the\n"
"sentence's Middle Kleene value is defined at every situation of the context.\n"
"\n"
"The statement below says exactly this, so §1 proves it: like §2, an §3 holds by §4 when\n"
"its two sides are the same by definition. The statement has a name, §5, and\n"
"once it is proved it joins your inventory."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Experiment.verdict`
#. §1: `correct`
#. §2: `wrong`
#. §3: `silent`
#. §4: `rw [Experiment.verdict]`
#: Game/Levels/Data/L03_Verdict.lean:8
msgid "A verdict compares a prediction with an observation (§0): §1 if they\n"
"agree, §2 if they differ, and §3 if either is missing. Unfold the definition with\n"
"§4, then rewrite with the results of the last two levels, which are now in\n"
"your inventory."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/OrderMatters/L02_UndefinednessFirst.lean:16
msgid "An undefined conjunct followed by a false one gives an undefined conjunction."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `meetWeak`
#: Game/Levels/OrderMatters/L05_WeakKleene.lean:8
msgid "Bochvar's internal logic, which is also Kleene's weak logic, treats the third value as infectious:\n"
"a conjunction is undefined as soon as either conjunct is. Linglib defines this conjunction as\n"
"§0. A false conjunct no longer rescues an undefined one in either position."
msgstr ""

